int protocol_write_line(int fd, const char *fmt, ...);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Formats a string using \f[CR]vsnprintf(3)\f[R] with
\f[CR]printf\f[R]\-style format specifiers, appends a newline character
(\f[CR]\(rsn\f[R]), and writes the result to the file descriptor
\f[CR]fd\f[R].
.PP
The function first attempts formatting into a stack\-allocated buffer of
\f[CR]SERVER_MAX_LINE\f[R] (8192) bytes.
If the formatted output exceeds this size (e.g., base64\-encoded
STDOUT/STDERR payloads up to \(ti1.4 MB), a heap buffer is dynamically
allocated to accommodate the full output.
.PP
Writing uses \f[CR]write(2)\f[R] in a loop to handle partial writes and
\f[CR]EINTR\f[R] interruptions.
.PP
This function is used for v1 text protocol responses.
For v2 framed I/O, see \f[CR]json_frame_write(3)\f[R] and
